ADDENDA <Act No. 11373, Feb. 22, 2012>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force three months after the date of its promulgation; provided, Articles 3 and 7 of the Addenda shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Repeal of other statutes)
The Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation Act is hereby repealed.
Article 3 (Establishment of Committee for Incorporation of Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation)
(1) The Chairperson of the Korea Communications Commission shall establish a committee for the incorporation of the Corporation (hereinafter referred to as the "Incorporation Committee") in order to handle administrative affairs necessary for the incorporation of the Corporation, the transfer of assets and business affairs of the Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation incorporated under the previous Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the "former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation"), the transfer of employees, and other similar matters.
(2) The Incorporation Committee shall be comprised of no more than five members commissioned by the Chairperson of the Korea Communications Commission, from among persons who have abundant knowledge of and experience in broadcasting, advertising, etc. and the chairperson of the Incorporation Committee shall be appointed by the Chairperson of the Korea Communications Commission, from among members of the Incorporation Committee. The Incorporation Committee may hire employees necessary for assistance to the Incorporation Committee in handling its business affairs.
(3) The Incorporation Committee shall prepare the Corporation's articles of incorporation, obtain approval thereof from the Chairperson of the Korea Communications Commission, and complete registration for the Corporation's incorporation by the date this Act enters into force.
(4) The Incorporation Committee shall transfer business affairs to the president of the Corporation without delay after completing registration for incorporation, and the Incorporation Committee shall be dissolved and members of the Incorporation Committee shall be deemed dismissed as at the time the transfer of business affairs is completed.
(5) Expenses incurred in the dissolution of the former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation and expenses incurred in the incorporation of the Corporation shall be borne by the Corporation.
(6) Matters necessary for the organization and operation of the committee for recommendation of executive officers for appointing the Corporation's executive officers to be appointed initially under this Act shall be determined by the Korea Communications Commission.
Article 4 (Special cases concerning broadcast advertising sales agencies)
Provisions regarding broadcast advertising sales agencies of general program providers prescribed in Article 5 shall apply three years after the date of approval of the general program providers. Each general program provider may file an application for permission for broadcast advertising sales agency business in such cases.
Article 5 (Applicability to small and medium terrestrial broadcasting business entities)
Articles 20 and 22 shall apply only to terrestrial broadcasting business entities for a local network, and small and medium terrestrial broadcasting program providers existing as at the time this Act enters into force.
Article 6 (General transitional measures)
A disposition, proceeding, or any other act made or done in accordance with the previous Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation Act before this Act enters into force shall be deemed made or done in accordance with this Act, unless such disposition, proceeding, or act does not contravene this Act.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning broadcast advertising sales agencies)
(1) A person who acts as sales agent for terrestrial broadcast advertising as at the time this Act enters into force shall obtain permission for an advertising sales agency within three months after the Enforcement Decree of this Act is promulgated.
(2) A person who falls under paragraph (1) shall assist the terrestrial broadcasting business entities for a local network, and small and medium terrestrial broadcasting program providers, whom he or she currently assist through combined sale, in accordance with Article 20(2), until before he or she obtains permission for an advertising sales agency.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning executive officers and employees of the Former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation)
(1) The Corporation shall appoint its executive officers within three months after this Act enters into force in accordance with this Act.
(2) The president, managing director, directors, and an auditor of the former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation as at the time this Act enters into force shall perform their duties until executive officers are appointed in accordance with this Act.
(3) Employees of the former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation as at the time the Corporation is established shall be deemed employees of the Corporation; provided, the foregoing shall not apply to employees who express written dissent thereto.
Article 9 (Transitional measures concerning succession to property, rights, and obligations of the Former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation)
(1) The Corporation shall succeed to all property, rights, claims, liabilities, rights, and obligations that belong to the former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation simultaneously when the Corporation is incorporated.
(2) The title of the former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation indicated in the register of property, rights, and obligations to which the Corporation succeeds and other official records shall be deemed the title of the Corporation simultaneously when the Corporation is incorporated.
(3) The value of the property to which the Corporation succeeds in accordance with paragraph (1) shall be the book value of the property as on the date preceding the date of incorporation of the Corporation.
(4) The Chairperson of the Korea Communications Commission shall consult with the Minister of Strategy and Finance and the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism within three months after this Act enters into force with respect to the management and operation of fixed assets, among the property to which the Corporation succeeds in accordance with paragraph (1).
Article 10 (Transitional measures concerning investment by government in Corporation)
(1) Residual funds after subtracting liabilities and other debts from the book value of the property to which the Corporation succeeds from the former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation in accordance with Article 9(1) of the Addenda shall be deemed invested by the State in the Corporation.
(2) The former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation shall be deemed dissolved simultaneously when the Corporation is incorporated, notwithstanding provisions regarding dissolution and liquidation in the Civil Act. The incorporation of the Corporation shall be deemed succession to the former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation as a result of the change in its legal personality.
(3) If necessary in connection with the dissolution and liquidation of the former Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation and the incorporation of the Corporation, the State or a local government may fully or partially exempt the Corporation from national or local taxes in accordance with the provisions of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, the Local Tax Act, and other relevant statutes.
Article 11 Omitted.
Article 12 (Relationship to other statutes and regulations)
(1) A citation to the previous Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation Act or a provision thereof by any other statute or regulation in force as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a citation to this Act or the relevant provision of this Act if such relevant provision exists herein.
(2) A citation of the previous Korea Broadcasting Advertising Corporation by any other statute or regulation in force as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a citation of the Corporation under this Act.

